invariant: INV-13
file: srv_tcp_nonblocking.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: the tcp-nonblocking server pushes no alert record when its handshake
  fails, so the client waits on a connection the server has closed without
  learning why. bin/tcp_nonblocking_loop_test requires each server failure to
  push one alert record through cfg.srv.on_record_out, which the client then
  reads.

--- old
    if (rec_len != 0) {
        (void)srv_out_record(&r->t, rec, rec_len);
    }
--- new
    (void)rec_len;
